---
const discovery = [
  {
    q: "How many photos?",
    a: "About 100",
    built: "Categories and subcategories, not one giant pile.",
  },
  {
    q: "How often will you add new ones?",
    a: "After almost every job",
    built: "Self-serve. He had to be able to post without help from anyone.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where are they?",
    a: "On my phone",
    built: "Mobile-first.",
  },
  {
    q: "Comfortable with tech?",
    a: "Not much, but it's easy to post on Instagram",
    built:
      "An upload flow as easy as posting to Instagram + Reinforced mobile-first.",
  },
];

const added = [
  {
    title: "Labels in Spanish.",
    why: "English isn't his first language and he's not great with tech, so every label is in Spanish, telling him exactly what to do.",
  },
  {
    title: "Free to run.",
    why: "He's a small business owner, so I kept his costs down. Nothing to pay to keep it online.",
  },
];

import Section from "./Section.astro";
import Prose from "./Prose.astro";
import Column from "./Column.astro";
---

<Section title="The Brief">
  <Prose>
    <p>
      A concrete and landscaping contractor in Bakersfield messaged me wanting
      his first website. For years his work had spread by word of mouth, and he
      had a phone full of proof: finished patios, driveways, backyards, etc. He
      just didn't have anywhere to send customers.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before writing any code, I needed to know what to build, not how. My first
      questions were too technical and only confused him, so I switched to asking
      about his work and how he'd use the site, and his answers set the spec.
    </p>
  </Prose>

  <Column class="mt-8">
    <ul class="space-y-3">
    {
      discovery.map((d) => (
        <li class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:gap-3">
            <span class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 sm:flex-1">
              {d.q}
            </span>
            <svg
              class="hidden h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0 text-violet-400 sm:block"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"
              />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-violet-700">{d.a}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-2.5 flex items-start gap-2 border-t border-gray-100 pt-2.5">
            <svg
              class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-amber-500"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M5 5v7a3 3 0 003 3h11m0 0l-4-4m4 4l-4 4"
              />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-sm font-medium text-amber-700">{d.built}</span>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
    </ul>
  </Column>

  <Column class="mt-8">
    <span
      class="text-xs font-semibold text-amber-700 tracking-widest uppercase"
    >
      What I added
    </span>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        added.map((r) => (
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 px-5 py-4">
            <h3 class="mb-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-amber-900">
              {r.title}
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-amber-800/80">{r.why}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </Column>
</Section>
